# motorfader: the DB8E shows the fader value, including a preset recall.
# Spec: motorfader.md "automatically updates the display whenever the virtual
# value of the fader changes (by user interaction)".
#
# MEASURED on hardware (issue #19): the parenthetical is not a restriction. A
# preset recall drives the MOTOR rather than the hand, and it still shows — the
# reading snaps straight to the recalled value rather than following the motor
# across. (The first draft of this circuit read "by user interaction" strictly
# and stayed silent on a recall; hardware says otherwise.)
#
# Header comes from the `output` target, an internal cable, so the leading
# underscore is dropped: "LEVEL".
#   t0: seeded at startvalue 0.4; nothing moved -> screen off
#   t1: user moves the fader to 0.8            -> shows 0.8
#   t2: save that into preset 0 (no value change, so nothing new to show)
#   t3: user moves to 0.2                      -> shows 0.2
#   t5: recall preset 0 -> the motor drives the fader back to 0.8 and the
#       screen follows it in the same tick
tickrate 100
patch <<<
[m4]
[db8e]

[motorfader]
    fader      = 1
    startvalue = 0.4
    savepreset = I1
    loadpreset = I2
    preset     = 0
    output     = _LEVEL

# The cable needs a reader.
[copy]
    input  = _LEVEL
    output = O1
>>>
@0 expectdisplay D1 off
@1 move F1 0.8
@1 expectdisplay D1 value 0.8 tol 1e-4
@1 expectdisplay D1 header "LEVEL"
@2 set I1 1
@2 expectdisplay D1 value 0.8 tol 1e-4
@3 set I1 0
@3 move F1 0.2
@3 expectdisplay D1 value 0.2 tol 1e-4
@5 set I2 1
@5 expect F1 0.8 tol 1e-4
@5 expectdisplay D1 value 0.8 tol 1e-4
@6 expectdisplay D1 value 0.8 tol 1e-4
